<a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>preinitiation complex</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2800" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t> (PIC) at the typical TATA box of a promoter</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:cxnSp><p:nvCxnSpPr><p:cNvPr id="654" name="Google Shape;654;p90"/><p:cNvCxnSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvCxnSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="304800" y="1143000"/><a:ext cx="8458200" cy="0"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="straightConnector1"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln cap="flat" cmpd="thinThick" w="57150"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:prstDash val="solid"/><a:miter lim="800000"/><a:headEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/><a:tailEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:cxnSp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr descr="A series of diagrams illustrating the components of transcriptional activation. Two blue lines that begin at the top left, extend down and curve right, where they are labeled DNA. To the right of the line right before it curves, there is a purple structure with two tan and purple bases, labeled Activator. Below this structure, the lines are shaded deeply and labeled as Enhancer. Inside the right side of the lines, there are two shaded areas, separated by a white space. The first section is slightly longer and purple, labeled TATA, and the second is orange, labeled lnr. Below this structure is an arrow pointing down, labeled Mediator. Below that is another arrow pointing down, labeled Modification and remodeling enzymes. Below the arrows is the same structure described previously, but this time, a green globular mass, labeled Modification and remodeling complex, is lodged on top of the activator, and to the top left of the green structure, a series of purple ovals that create one large mass, labeled Mediator, is attached. Below that is an arrow pointing down, labeled TBP and TFIIB. Below that is a structure similar to the one described, but this time, where the TATA and lnr are on the lines, it dips up and is attached to a dark green structure labeled TFIIB, a brow ovular structure labeled TBP. The Mediator serves as a bridge to this complex of structures and the modification and remodeling complex. The TATA is lodged up into the brown ovular structure. Below that is a series of six arrows, labeled TFIID, TFIIA, TFIIB, TFIIF-Pol II, TFIIE, and TFIIH. Below that is a structure similar to the one just described, but this time, a yellow complex that is labeled TBP on the left, TFIIA (in the middle white section), and TFIID to the bottom right, surrounds the structures that are connected to the blue lines near TATA. Above the TFIID is a tan ovular structure labeled Pol II, and on top of it is a brown kidney shaped structure with a handle, labeled TFIIF. The top of the handle connects to a purple boomerang structure labeled TFIIE, which sits above the top part of Pol II. A tan handle sits to the left of TFIIE; this is labeled CTD. To the right of TFIIE is a long gray structure that is larger than the others; it has an opening at the top, in the center. To its right, a small section of the blue lines is shown.&#xA;" id="655" name="Google Shape;655;p90"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill rotWithShape="1"><a:blip r:embed="rId3"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:srcRect b="0" l="0" r="0" t="0"/><a:stretch/></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="5715000" y="1295400"/><a:ext cx="2133600" cy="5416550"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:pic></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>